# the macros (v0.2): offsets on top of the sound, the sound's own values untouched; each part comes in over its own
# stretch of the way in and goes over its own on the way out, gliding (0.6 s at most). heardN is what's heard (the
# sound plus the macros), parN the sound's own, mpitchG a drone's pitch move by the macros (cents). 7 drone I's
# cutoff, 5 its osc mix, 25 drone II's detune, 63 the reverb mix, 44 hard sync, 42 cross-mod;
# 78-81 Bloom, Weight, Tide, Tear; 82-85 the gestures' depths (83: Shift's move), 86-89 their swells, 90-93 their
# latches (Weight, Shift, Converge, Wash on D5-G5: w12-w15).
tap PLAY
wait 1000
expect heard7 700
# SEQ: the Macros page. Bloom at 100: the cutoffs +220, the reverb mix +30 (35 to start); the knob's own value stays
tap SEQ
expect view 8
spin K1 100
wait 700
expect par78 100
expect par7 700
expect heard7 920
expect heard63 65
spin K1 -100
wait 700
expect heard7 700
# the page's Weight at 100: the sub +45
spin K2 100
wait 700
expect par79 100
expect heard5 75
spin K2 -100
wait 700
expect heard5 30
# PRESETS: Macro time (50: each gesture's own time); no macro's amount moves
spin PRESET 10
expect mtime 60
expect par78 0
spin PRESET -10
expect mtime 50
# Tear: hard sync on from its first step
spin K4 1
wait 100
expect heard44 1
spin K4 -1
wait 700
expect heard44 0
# WEIGHT held swells in (2.8 s), a warm bass: half way, the cutoff most of the way down (by 30 at most), the sub
# half way up
key w12 down
wait 1400
expect heard7 <690
expect heard5 >50
expect heard5 <70
wait 1500
expect heard5 >62
key w12 up
wait 1000
expect heard7 >680
expect heard5 >38
wait 2500
expect heard5 30
expect heard7 700
# let go after a short hold: it goes over as long as it was held (1 s), not its own time
key w12 down
wait 1000
key w12 up
expect heard5 >38
wait 1100
expect heard5 30
# let go after a long hold (5 s, in by 2.8 s): it drifts out over 5 s
key w12 down
wait 5000
key w12 up
wait 2500
expect heard5 >38
wait 3000
expect heard5 30
# Macro time x0.1 (PRESETS all the way down): in by about 0.3 s
spin PRESET -50
expect mtime 0
key w12 down
wait 400
expect heard5 >70
key w12 up
wait 600
expect heard5 30
spin PRESET 50
expect mtime 50
# a tap: to its depth, and it stays; a tap again: it goes
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 100
expect heard5 >62
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 0
expect heard5 30
# SEL held as you let go: latched where it is
key w12 down
wait 1000
press SEL
key w12 up
release SEL
expect par90 >20
expect par90 <60
tapkey w12
wait 4000
expect par90 0
# SHIFT: held, ALGORITHM picks its move (a 4th down), PRESETS its own time (3.9 s, 4 shorter: 3.4 s)
key w13 down
spin ALGO 2
spin PRESET -4
wait 300
key w13 up
expect par83 2
expect par87 36
expect par75 50
wait 4000
expect mpitch0 0
expect mpitch1 0
# tapped: drone I glides down a 4th first, drone II after it
tapkey w13
wait 1500
expect mpitch0 <-250
expect mpitch1 >-100
wait 3000
expect mpitch0 -500
expect mpitch1 -500
tapkey w13
wait 4500
expect mpitch0 0
expect mpitch1 0
# CONVERGE: drone II's pitch toward a consonance with drone I first (drone I stepping back, quieter, meanwhile),
# never quite there (a few cents short, so they pulse; here they're a fifth already), cross-mod last (3.3 s)
expect heard11 80
key w14 down
wait 1000
expect heard42 0
expect heard11 <72
wait 3000
expect heard42 1
expect heard25 5
expect mpitch1 <-3
expect mpitch1 >-16
expect heard11 80
key w14 up
wait 4500
expect heard42 0
expect mpitch1 0
# a scene keeps the macros: A1 stored with Bloom 40 and Wash latched, recalled from none
spin K1 40
tapkey w15
wait 7000
press SAVE
tapkey w0
release SAVE
wait 300
spin K1 -40
tapkey w15
wait 7000
expect par78 0
expect par93 0
tapkey w0
wait 7000
expect par78 40
expect par93 100
expect heard7 777
# a restart brings the whole sound back to the engine, the macros too (the last values of a load were
# once dropped)
tap SAVE
wait 500
reboot
wait 500
expect par78 40
expect heard7 777
# SAVE again with nothing changed: nothing is written (each write is a late block while playing)
expect store_writes 1
tap SAVE
wait 500
expect store_writes 1
